From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:46:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 072/342] MediaPlayer: go back to the frame after switching the
 decoded format

MediaTrackVideoSupplier::SwitchFormat(), which the Controller uses to
have the video decoded to B_YCbCr422 for overlays that need it (since
35c1a61529), makes the decoder negotiate again. The ffmpeg plugin then
reopens the codec and decodes a frame to settle the format, from where
the track is: after the packets the old format's first frame took. A
codec started there throws away everything up to the next keyframe, and
playback began at that keyframe. With B-frames that is often the next
IDR frame, 8.3 s into a file x264 made: the picture ran 8.3 s ahead of
the sound, and stood still at the end until the sound caught up. Without
B-frames it was the next scene cut, typically a second or so.

SwitchFormat() now seeks the track back to the frame it was at (frame 0
before playback); the plugin's SeekedTo() flushes the codec and drops the
frame decoded for the negotiation.

Measured on the ODROID-C2 with the HDMI capture, a clip with a flash and
a beep at irregular times: sound 8.32-8.34 s after the picture before,
-7..+19 ms after (the capture path itself shows sound 50-150 ms early).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.cpp      | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.h        |  4 +---
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.cpp b/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.cpp
index 96931a158c..473e17fa4f 100644
--- a/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.cpp
+++ b/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.cpp
@@ -286,6 +286,29 @@ MediaTrackVideoSupplier::BytesPerRow() const
 // #pragma mark -
 
 
+status_t
+MediaTrackVideoSupplier::SwitchFormat(color_space format, uint32 bytesPerRow)
+{
+	status_t status = _SwitchFormat(format, bytesPerRow);
+	if (status != B_OK)
+		return status;
+
+	// To settle the new format, the decoder decodes a frame, from where the
+	// track is: after the packets it took for the old format's first frame.
+	// A codec started over there throws away everything up to the next
+	// keyframe (with B-frames often the next IDR frame, seconds later), and
+	// playback then started there: the picture ran that far ahead of the
+	// sound, and stood still at the end until the sound caught up. Go back.
+	int64 frame = fCurrentFrame;
+	if (fVideoTrack->SeekToFrame(&frame, B_MEDIA_SEEK_CLOSEST_BACKWARD)
+			== B_OK) {
+		fCurrentFrame = fVideoTrack->CurrentFrame();
+		fPerformanceTime = fVideoTrack->CurrentTime();
+	}
+	return B_OK;
+}
+
+
 status_t
 MediaTrackVideoSupplier::_SwitchFormat(color_space format, uint32 bytesPerRow)
 {
diff --git a/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.h b/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.h
index 299fabd1f0..1f85756551 100644
--- a/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.h
+++ b/src/apps/mediaplayer/supplier/MediaTrackVideoSupplier.h
@@ -44,9 +44,7 @@ class MediaTrackVideoSupplier : public VideoTrackSupplier {
 	virtual	uint32				BytesPerRow() const;
 
 	virtual	status_t			SwitchFormat(color_space format,
-									uint32 bytesPerRow)
-									{ return _SwitchFormat(format,
-										bytesPerRow); }
+									uint32 bytesPerRow);
 
 	virtual	int32				TrackIndex() const
 									{ return fTrackIndex; }
